{# How to name a document in a call. The failed reads give a file name, a path or a hash of
   the wrong length in place of the file_hash. #}
Naming a document

A document hash has 64 hexadecimal characters. Copy it with its collection name from a search result.

1. Copy the file_hash and the collectionname of the same result row. Never write a hash yourself, and never shorten it or add a character.
2. {% if has('read_documents') %}{{ tool('read_documents') }} can also resolve a file name or path when it names one document.{% endif %} Other document tools use the hash.
3. To find the file_hash of a file by its name, search for the name with {{ tool('search_collections') }}{% if has('folder_search') %} or {{ tool('folder_search') }}{% endif %}, and copy the file_hash of the row.
{% if has('read_more') %}
4. When a row has no file_hash, call {{ tool('read_more') }} for the next page of the result.
{% endif %}

When a read says that no readable dataset holds a hash, the hash is wrong or it belongs to another collection. Do not send it again. Copy the hash and the collectionname again from the row, or search again.
